BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Trace the chronological evolution of electronic devices from thermionic vacuum tubes to modern 3nm Gate-All-Around \(GAAFET\) field-effect transistors, detailing key operational mechanisms and technological bottlenecks.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Thermionic Vacuum Tube Era \(1904 - 1947\):) Tj
T*
(   - Thermionic Diode \(Fleming Valve, 1904\): Based on Edison's thermionic emission effect, where a) Tj
T*
(   heated filament cathode releases free electrons in a vacuum, collected by a positively biased) Tj
T*
(   anode plate. It enabled the first electrical AC rectification and wireless RF detection.) Tj
T*
(   - Triode \(Lee de Forest Audion, 1906\): Inserted an electrostatic wire mesh \(control grid\)) Tj
T*
(   between cathode and anode. Small voltage variations on the grid modulated the large plate) Tj
T*
(   current, achieving the first electrical signal amplification. Subsequent tetrodes and pentodes) Tj
T*
(   solved inter-electrode Miller capacitance and secondary emission.) Tj
T*
(   - Bottlenecks: Bulky glass envelopes, fragile filaments, excessive heating power \(dozens of) Tj
T*
(   watts per tube\), high operating plate voltages \(100V-400V\), and limited mean time between) Tj
T*
(   failures \(MTBF < a few thousand hours\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Solid-State Transistor & Integrated Circuit Revolution \(1947 - 1970s\):) Tj
T*
(   - Point-Contact Transistor \(Bardeen, Brattain, Shockley, Bell Labs, 1947\): Demonstrated) Tj
T*
(   solid-state amplification using two gold foil contacts pressed onto a germanium crystal slice.) Tj
T*
(   Shockley subsequently formulated the theory of the Bipolar Junction Transistor \(BJT, 1948\).) Tj
T*
(   - Planar Process & Integrated Circuits \(Kilby 1958, Noyce & Hoerni 1959\): Silicon dioxide) Tj
T*
(   thermal passivation and photolithography enabled multiple transistors, diodes, and resistors to) Tj
T*
(   be fabricated simultaneously on a single monolithic silicon wafer, terminating discrete) Tj
T*
(   component assembly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Silicon MOSFET Scaling and Architectural Evolution \(1970s - Present\):) Tj
T*
(   - Planar MOSFET Scaling \(1970s - 2011\): Scaled according to Dennard scaling until short-channel) Tj
T*
(   effects \(DIBL, subthreshold leakage, and gate dielectric tunneling\) halted planar progress) Tj
T*
(   below 20nm.) Tj
T*
(   - 3D FinFET Architecture \(Intel 2011, TSMC\): Replaced flat planar gates with vertical silicon) Tj
T*
(   fins wrapped on three sides by the gate dielectric, dramatically boosting electrostatic control) Tj
T*
(   and suppressing leakage currents.) Tj
T*
(   - Gate-All-Around Nanosheet FET \(GAAFET, sub-3nm nodes\): Vertically stacked silicon nanosheets) Tj
T*
(   surrounded on all four sides by gate metal. This provides maximum electrostatic channel) Tj
T*
(   pinch-off, superior drive current per footprint, and enables continued scaling toward 1nm) Tj
T*
(   Complementary FET \(CFET\) architectures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate Moore's Law and Dennard Scaling, analyze the thermodynamic and quantum mechanical physical limits that caused Dennard scaling breakdown, and explain modern architectural remedies.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Foundations of Scaling Laws:) Tj
T*
(   - Moore's Law \(Gordon Moore, 1965\): An economic and empirical principle stating that the number) Tj
T*
(   of transistors on a dense integrated circuit doubles approximately every 18 to 24 months,) Tj
T*
(   accompanied by an exponential drop in cost per transistor function.) Tj
T*
(   - Dennard Scaling \(Robert Dennard, 1974\): Predicted that as transistor dimensions \(channel) Tj
T*
(   length L, width W, oxide thickness tox\) scale down by a constant factor k \(where k > 1,) Tj
T*
(   typically 1.4 per node\), operating voltage Vdd and threshold voltage Vt must scale by 1/k.) Tj
T*
(   Under these conditions, the circuit delay improves by 1/k, transistor density increases by k^2,) Tj
T*
(   but power density \(Power / Area\) remains constant, enabling higher clock frequencies without) Tj
T*
(   thermal runaway.) Tj
T*
ET

