(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the comprehensive 9-stage engineering lifecycle of an Application-Specific Integrated Circuit \(ASIC\) from architectural specification to silicon tape-out.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Stage 1: Product Architecture & System Specification:) Tj
T*
(   - Define performance metrics \(throughput, clock frequency, latency\), power consumption budget) Tj
T*
(   \(dynamic and leakage\), silicon die area targets, memory hierarchy, and external I/O protocols) Tj
T*
(   \(PCIe, DDR5, USB4\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Stage 2: Register-Transfer Level \(RTL\) Design:) Tj
T*
(   - Author synthesizable hardware models in SystemVerilog, Verilog, or VHDL. Partition design) Tj
T*
(   into modular datapaths and finite state machines \(FSMs\), adhering to synchronous design) Tj
T*
(   principles.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Stage 3: Functional Verification & Simulation:) Tj
T*
(   - Develop modular, reusable testbenches using Universal Verification Methodology \(UVM\). Employ) Tj
T*
(   constrained-random stimulus generation, functional coverage metrics, and SystemVerilog) Tj
T*
(   Assertions \(SVA\) to verify design compliance and uncover corner-case microarchitectural bugs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Stage 4: Logic Synthesis:) Tj
T*
(   - Automated synthesis tools \(e.g., Synopsys Design Compiler\) map RTL constructs into a) Tj
T*
(   gate-level netlist of interconnected standard cells \(NAND, NOR, flip-flops\) optimized for) Tj
T*
(   target foundry process libraries while meeting area, power, and timing constraints.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Stage 5: Design for Testability \(DFT\) Insertion:) Tj
T*
(   - Integrate internal test logic: scan flip-flop chains, Built-In Self-Test \(BIST\) controllers) Tj
T*
(   for embedded SRAM arrays, and boundary scan JTAG \(IEEE 1149.1\) architecture to ensure silicon) Tj
T*
(   defects can be diagnosed post-manufacturing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   6. Stage 6: Static Timing Analysis \(STA\):) Tj
T*
(   - Verify setup and hold timing across all operating process, voltage, and temperature \(PVT\)) Tj
T*
(   corners using tools like Synopsys PrimeTime without requiring dynamic test vectors.) Tj
T*
