(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the concept of Short-Channel Effects \(SCE\) in sub-micron planar MOSFETs, detailing DIBL, velocity saturation, hot-carrier degradation, and how FinFET technology solves these issues.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Manifestation of Short-Channel Effects:) Tj
T*
(   - When the physical channel length L of a planar MOSFET is scaled down to dimensions comparable) Tj
T*
(   to the source and drain depletion region widths, 1D gate electrostatic control is undermined by) Tj
T*
(   2D electric field fringing from the drain.) Tj
T*
(   - Drain-Induced Barrier Lowering \(DIBL\): At high drain bias Vds, the drain's electric field) Tj
T*
(   penetrates deep into the channel, pulling down the electrostatic potential barrier at the) Tj
T*
(   source edge. This causes threshold voltage Vt to roll off rapidly with channel length \(Vt) Tj
T*
(   roll-off\) and creates severe subthreshold leakage currents when the device is OFF.) Tj
T*
(   - Velocity Saturation: High lateral electric fields \(E > 10^4 V/cm\) cause carrier drift) Tj
T*
(   velocity to saturate due to optical phonon scattering, reducing saturation drain current from) Tj
T*
(   quadratic \(Id ~ \(Vgs-Vt\)^2\) to linear \(Id ~ \(Vgs-Vt\)\), eliminating transconductance gains from) Tj
T*
(   scaling.) Tj
T*
(   - Hot Carrier Injection \(HCI\): High-energy electrons accelerated by severe electric fields near) Tj
T*
(   the drain impact-ionize lattice atoms and inject into the SiO2 gate dielectric, creating) Tj
T*
(   permanent interface traps that shift Vt over time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The 3D FinFET Architecture Solution:) Tj
T*
(   - Structural Redesign: Instead of a planar conduction plane, the silicon channel is extruded) Tj
T*
(   vertically into an ultra-thin 3D silicon fin \(thickness Wfin < 10 nm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Tri-Gate Electrostatic Enclosure: The gate dielectric and metal electrode wrap around the top) Tj
T*
(   and both vertical sidewalls of the fin. Because the gate surrounds the channel on three sides,) Tj
T*
(   gate electric field lines dominate the internal potential from three directions simultaneously.) Tj
T*
(   - Channel Depletion: The body of the fin is made so thin that it is fully depleted of mobile) Tj
T*
(   carriers without requiring heavy channel dopant atoms \(eliminating Random Dopant Fluctuation -) Tj
T*
(   RDF\). DIBL is drastically curtailed, subthreshold swing approaches the ideal 60 mV/decade) Tj
T*
(   limit, and leakage current drops by up to 90%.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
