T*
(   1. Ray Optics and Waveguide Physics:) Tj
T*
(   - Total Internal Reflection \(TIR\): An optical fiber consists of a cylindrical silica glass core) Tj
T*
(   \(refractive index n1\) surrounded by a cladding \(refractive index n2\), where n1 > n2. When light) Tj
T*
(   strikes the core-cladding interface at an angle of incidence greater than the critical angle) Tj
T*
(   theta_c = arcsin\(n2 / n1\), 100% of the optical energy reflects internally without refraction) Tj
T*
(   loss.) Tj
T*
(   - Numerical Aperture \(NA\): The light-gathering capacity of the fiber from air \(n0 = 1\): NA =) Tj
T*
(   sin\(theta_max\) = sqrt\(n1^2 - n2^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Single-Mode Fiber \(SMF\): By shrinking core diameter to ~8 to 9 micrometers, only the) Tj
T*
(   fundamental transverse electromagnetic mode \(LP01\) can propagate, completely eliminating) Tj
T*
(   intermodal dispersion that degrades multi-mode fibers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Fiber Loss and Attenuation Mechanisms:) Tj
T*
(   - Rayleigh Scattering: Microscopic density and compositional fluctuations frozen into the glass) Tj
T*
(   lattice during drawing scatter light in all directions. Attenuation varies inversely with the) Tj
T*
(   fourth power of wavelength \(Loss ~ 1 / lambda^4\), causing high loss in ultraviolet/visible) Tj
T*
(   light and minimal loss in the infrared spectrum.) Tj
T*
(   - Absorption Losses: Intrinsic ultraviolet and infrared absorption bands of SiO2, combined with) Tj
T*
(   extrinsic absorption from residual water hydroxyl ions \(OH- absorption peak around 1383 nm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Wavelength Windows: Standard telecom fibers achieve minimum dispersion at 1310 nm \(~0.35) Tj
T*
(   dB/km\) and absolute minimum attenuation in the C-band at 1550 nm \(~0.20 dB/km\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Chromatic Dispersion and Mitigation:) Tj
T*
(   - Chromatic Dispersion: Different spectral components of an optical pulse travel at different) Tj
T*
