(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the timing constraints in digital synchronous circuits, deriving mathematical equations for setup time, hold time, clock skew, and maximum achievable operating clock frequency.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Fundamental Circuit Timing Parameters:) Tj
T*
(   - Clock Period \(Tclk\): Time duration between consecutive active clock edges \(f_clk = 1 / Tclk\).) Tj
T*
(   - Clock-to-Q Propagation Delay \(tco\): Time elapsed from the active clock edge at Register 1) Tj
T*
(   until valid data emerges at output Q.) Tj
T*
(   - Combinational Logic Delay \(tlogic\): Propagation delay through combinational gates between) Tj
T*
(   Register 1 and Register 2 \(bounded by tlogic_max and tlogic_min\).) Tj
T*
(   - Setup Time \(tsu\): Minimum duration data at Register 2's input D must be stable prior to the) Tj
T*
(   active clock edge.) Tj
T*
(   - Hold Time \(th\): Minimum duration data at Register 2's input D must remain stable after the) Tj
T*
(   active clock edge.) Tj
T*
(   - Clock Skew \(tskew\): Difference in clock arrival times at destination and source flip-flops:) Tj
T*
(   tskew = tclk_dest - tclk_src.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Setup Time Constraint \(Maximum Frequency Formulation\):) Tj
T*
(   - For data launched by Register 1 on clock edge n to be safely latched by Register 2 on clock) Tj
T*
(   edge n+1, data must arrive at least tsu before the destination clock edge:) Tj
T*
(   tclk_src + tco_max + tlogic_max <= tclk_dest + Tclk - tsu.) Tj
T*
(   Tclk >= tco_max + tlogic_max + tsu - \(tclk_dest - tclk_src\) = tco_max + tlogic_max + tsu -) Tj
T*
(   tskew.) Tj
T*
(   - Maximum Operating Frequency: f_max = 1 / \(tco_max + tlogic_max + tsu - tskew\).) Tj
T*
(   - Positive skew \(clock arrives later at destination\) relaxes setup time, while negative skew) Tj
T*
(   degrades maximum clock frequency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Hold Time Constraint \(Race Condition Formulation\):) Tj
T*
(   - Data launched on clock edge n must not travel so rapidly that it overwrites data being) Tj
T*
(   sampled at Register 2 on the same clock edge n before its hold time expires:) Tj
T*
(   tclk_src + tco_min + tlogic_min >= tclk_dest + th.) Tj
T*
(   tco_min + tlogic_min >= th + tskew.) Tj
T*
(   - Hold Slack: Slack_hold = \(tco_min + tlogic_min\) - \(th + tskew\).) Tj
T*
(   - Crucial Engineering Insight: The hold time constraint is completely independent of clock) Tj
T*
(   period Tclk! A hold violation cannot be rectified by slowing down the clock. If Slack_hold < 0,) Tj
T*
(   the chip is permanently defective unless physical delay buffer cells are inserted into the) Tj
T*
(   combinational data path.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
