/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 13:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the theoretical and mathematical foundations of Discrete Fourier Transforms \(DFT\), and analyze how the Cooley-Tukey Fast Fourier Transform \(FFT\) algorithm revolutionizes digital signal processing.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Formulation of the Discrete Fourier Transform \(DFT\):) Tj
T*
(   - The DFT transforms an N-point discrete-time sequence x[n] into an N-point frequency-domain) Tj
T*
(   spectrum X[k]:) Tj
T*
(   X[k] = sum_{n=0}^{N-1} x[n] * W_N^{k * n}, for k = 0, 1, ..., N-1,) Tj
T*
(   where W_N = exp\(-j * 2 * pi / N\) is the complex twiddle factor.) Tj
T*
(   - Computational Complexity of Direct DFT: For each of the N frequency bins X[k], evaluating the) Tj
T*
(   sum requires N complex multiplications and \(N - 1\) complex additions. Computing all N bins) Tj
T*
(   requires N * N = N^2 complex multiplications and N * \(N - 1\) =~ N^2 complex additions. For N =) Tj
T*
(   1024 points, direct computation demands 1,048,576 complex multiplications, rendering real-time) Tj
T*
(   embedded DSP impractical.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Cooley-Tukey Radix-2 Decimation-in-Time FFT Algorithm:) Tj
T*
(   - Mathematical Symmetry Exploitation: The twiddle factor possesses periodic \(W_N^{k+N} = W_N^k\)) Tj
T*
(   and symmetry properties \(W_N^{k + N/2} = -W_N^k\).) Tj
T*
(   - Divide-and-Conquer Decomposition: Decomposes the N-point sum into two N/2-point DFTs?one for) Tj
T*
(   even-indexed samples x[2m] and one for odd-indexed samples x[2m+1]:) Tj
T*
(   X[k] = E[k] + W_N^k * O[k],) Tj
T*
(   X[k + N/2] = E[k] - W_N^k * O[k].) Tj
T*
(   - The Butterfly Operation: Each basic 2-point butterfly computes two outputs from two inputs) Tj
T*
(   using a single complex multiplication and two additions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
