(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate transmission line theory at high frequencies, define characteristic impedance Z0, reflection coefficient Gamma, and Voltage Standing Wave Ratio \(VSWR\), illustrating the critical importance of impedance matching.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Transition from Lumped to Distributed Circuit Theory:) Tj
T*
(   - At low frequencies \(e.g., 50 Hz power\), circuit dimensions are infinitesimal compared to) Tj
T*
(   signal wavelength \(L << lambda\), allowing Kirchhoff's laws to apply uniformly.) Tj
T*
(   - At RF and microwave frequencies \(e.g., GHz range, lambda in cm or mm\), signal phase changes) Tj
T*
(   significantly along physical wire lengths \(L >= 0.1 * lambda\). Wires must be modeled as) Tj
T*
(   distributed transmission lines characterized by per-unit-length inductance L', capacitance C',) Tj
T*
(   resistance R', and conductance G'.) Tj
T*
(   - Characteristic Impedance \(Z0\): The ratio of forward-traveling voltage wave to) Tj
T*
(   forward-traveling current wave in a uniform line:) Tj
T*
(   Z0 = sqrt\( \(R' + j * omega * L'\) / \(G' + j * omega * C'\) \). For lossless lines \(R'=0, G'=0\), Z0) Tj
T*
(   = sqrt\(L' / C'\), which is real and independent of line length \(standardized at 50 Ohms\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Reflection Coefficient and Wave Mismatch:) Tj
T*
(   - When an incident wave encounters a load impedance ZL that differs from Z0, boundary) Tj
T*
(   conditions require energy conservation via a reflected wave.) Tj
T*
(   - Voltage Reflection Coefficient \(Gamma\): Defined at the load as:) Tj
T*
(   Gamma = \(ZL - Z0\) / \(ZL + Z0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Extreme Cases: Matched Load \(ZL = Z0\) -> Gamma = 0 \(zero reflection\); Short Circuit \(ZL = 0\)) Tj
T*
(   -> Gamma = -1 \(complete inverted reflection\); Open Circuit \(ZL = infinity\) -> Gamma = +1) Tj
T*
(   \(complete in-phase reflection\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Voltage Standing Wave Ratio \(VSWR\) and Power Impact:) Tj
T*
(   - Interference between incident and reflected waves creates a stationary spatial standing wave) Tj
T*
(   pattern featuring voltage maxima \(Vmax = |V_inc| * \(1 + |Gamma|\)\) and minima \(Vmin = |V_inc| *) Tj
T*
(   \(1 - |Gamma|\)\).) Tj
T*
(   - VSWR: VSWR = Vmax / Vmin = \(1 + |Gamma|\) / \(1 - |Gamma|\).) Tj
T*
(   - Engineering Hazards of High VSWR: Reflected RF power \(|Gamma|^2 * P_inc\) returns toward the) Tj
T*
(   transmitter, causing severe heating and potentially destroying expensive RF power amplifier) Tj
T*
(   transistors. It also distorts pulse shapes and degrades receiver signal-to-noise ratio.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
