(   - In an open dipole antenna, oscillating RF currents drive charge accumulation at the antenna) Tj
T*
(   tips. As the polarity alternates, electric field lines detach and propagate outward into free) Tj
T*
(   space as self-sustaining transverse electromagnetic waves.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Field Regions Around an Antenna:) Tj
T*
(   - Reactive Near-Field \(R < 0.62 * sqrt\(D^3 / lambda\)\): Energy is stored reactively in inductive) Tj
T*
(   and capacitive fields without net radiating power.) Tj
T*
(   - Radiating Near-Field \(Fresnel Region: 0.62 * sqrt\(D^3 / lambda\) <= R < 2 * D^2 / lambda\):) Tj
T*
(   Radiation pattern varies with radial distance.) Tj
T*
(   - Far-Field \(Fraunhofer Region: R >= 2 * D^2 / lambda, where D is largest antenna dimension\):) Tj
T*
(   Wavefronts become essentially planar, angular radiation pattern is independent of distance, and) Tj
T*
(   electric and magnetic fields are strictly transverse and orthogonal with wave impedance eta0 =) Tj
T*
(   377 Ohms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Antenna Performance Metrics:) Tj
T*
(   - Radiation Pattern of Half-Wave Dipole: The normalized far-field E-plane pattern is F\(theta\) =) Tj
T*
(   [ cos\( \(pi/2\) * cos\(theta\) \) ] / sin\(theta\), forming an omnidirectional 'doughnut' pattern in) Tj
T*
(   3D space.) Tj
T*
(   - Directivity \(D\) and Gain \(G\): Directivity measures the concentration of radiated power in a) Tj
T*
(   specific direction compared to an isotropic radiator \(D_dipole = 1.64 or 2.15 dBi\). Realized) Tj
T*
(   Gain includes radiation efficiency eta_rad: G = eta_rad * D.) Tj
T*
(   - Effective Aperture \(A_eff\): The equivalent physical area that collects incoming RF power) Tj
T*
(   density: A_eff = \(lambda^2 / \(4 * pi\)\) * G.) Tj
T*
