(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the sensor fusion architecture in autonomous vehicles and robotics, explaining how radar, LiDAR, cameras, and Kalman filters cooperate to construct a reliable spatial perception model.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Autonomous Vehicle Sensing Modalities and Trade-offs:) Tj
T*
(   - Automotive Cameras: High-resolution visual capture \(RGB/monochrome\) providing rich color,) Tj
T*
(   semantic texture, traffic sign recognition, and lane boundary detection. However, cameras fail) Tj
T*
(   in adverse weather \(heavy fog, blinding glare, blizzard, darkness\) and cannot measure velocity) Tj
T*
(   directly.) Tj
T*
(   - Automotive Millimeter-Wave Radar \(77-81 GHz\): Penetrates rain, fog, dust, and darkness.) Tj
T*
(   Directly measures target range and Doppler radial velocity instantaneously using) Tj
T*
(   Frequency-Modulated Continuous-Wave \(FMCW\) chirps. However, radar has coarse angular resolution) Tj
T*
(   and struggles with non-metallic clutter.) Tj
T*
(   - Automotive LiDAR \(Light Detection and Ranging, 905nm or 1550nm\): Emits millions of pulsed) Tj
T*
(   laser beams per second, measuring time-of-flight to generate dense, geometrically accurate 3D) Tj
T*
(   point clouds \(<1 cm accuracy\). However, LiDAR is expensive and suffers attenuation in heavy fog) Tj
T*
(   or snow.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Sensor Fusion Hierarchy:) Tj
T*
(   - Low-Level / Early Fusion: Raw sensor data \(camera pixels + LiDAR point clouds\) are) Tj
T*
(   concatenated before feature extraction. Requires immense processing bandwidth and precise) Tj
T*
(   temporal synchronization.) Tj
T*
(   - High-Level / Object-Level Fusion: Each sensor subsystem independently runs object detection) Tj
T*
(   pipelines, outputting bounding boxes, velocities, and confidence scores. A central fusion) Tj
T*
(   engine combines these tracks, mitigating single-sensor failure.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. The Extended Kalman Filter \(EKF\) State Estimation Engine:) Tj
T*
(   - State Vector Definition: Tracks vehicle position, heading, velocity, and acceleration: x =) Tj
T*
(   [p_x, p_y, v_x, v_y, psi, psi_dot]^T.) Tj
T*
(   - Prediction Phase: Uses kinematic vehicle motion models and inertial measurement unit \(IMU\)) Tj
T*
(   gyro/accelerometer data to predict the future state and error covariance P.) Tj
T*
(   - Update Phase: When asynchronous sensor measurements arrive \(e.g., radar range, camera) Tj
T*
(   bounding box\), the EKF computes the Kalman Gain K = P * H^T * \(H * P * H^T + R\)^-1, optimally) Tj
T*
(   weighting model prediction against sensor measurement based on noise covariance R to deliver an) Tj
T*
(   uninterrupted, highly accurate spatial trajectory.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
