(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the physical principles and lithographic innovations of Extreme Ultraviolet \(EUV\) lithography systems, detailing the 13.5nm source, reflective multi-layer optics, and Pellicle challenges.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Resolution Limit of Optical Lithography:) Tj
T*
(   - Rayleigh's Resolution Criterion governs the minimum resolvable feature pitch in semiconductor) Tj
T*
(   photolithography: CD = k1 * \(lambda / NA\), where lambda is exposure wavelength, NA is numerical) Tj
T*
(   aperture, and k1 is process factor.) Tj
T*
(   - Deep Ultraviolet \(DUV\) lithography reached physical limits using 193 nm Argon Fluoride \(ArF\)) Tj
T*
(   excimer lasers. Even with liquid water immersion \(NA = 1.35\) and complex multi-patterning) Tj
T*
(   \(SADP, SAQP\), manufacturing sub-7nm features became prohibitively expensive and error-prone.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Extreme Ultraviolet \(EUV\) Technology \(lambda = 13.5 nm\):) Tj
T*
(   - Laser-Produced Plasma \(LPP\) Light Source: Molten tin \(Sn\) droplets \(~25 micrometers diameter\)) Tj
T*
(   are fired across a vacuum chamber at 50,000 droplets per second. A high-power pulsed CO2) Tj
T*
(   industrial laser vaporizes each tin droplet into high-temperature plasma, ionizing tin atoms to) Tj
T*
(   emit 13.5 nm EUV radiation.) Tj
T*
(   - All-Reflective Multi-Layer Optics: EUV radiation is absorbed by virtually all matter,) Tj
T*
(   including ambient air and optical glass. The entire scanner operates in ultra-high vacuum.) Tj
T*
(   Optical focusing lenses are replaced with specialized curved mirrors coated with 40 to 50) Tj
T*
(   alternating nanoscale layers of Molybdenum \(Mo\) and Silicon \(Si\). These act as Bragg) Tj
T*
(   reflectors, achieving ~70% reflectivity per mirror.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. EUV Photomask and Pellicle Engineering:) Tj
T*
(   - Reflective Photomasks: Masks utilize Mo/Si multi-layers on low-thermal-expansion substrates) Tj
T*
(   with tantalum-based patterned absorbers.) Tj
T*
(   - EUV Pellicle: A thin protective membrane positioned above the photomask to prevent airborne) Tj
T*
(   dust particles from settling on the focal pattern. Pellicles must be made of carbon nanotube or) Tj
T*
(   polysilicon films thinner than 50 nm that transmit >90% EUV light while withstanding intense) Tj
T*
(   thermal stress \(>300 W EUV source power without tearing\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
