(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the mathematical model of Orthogonal Frequency Division Multiplexing \(OFDM\), explaining subcarrier orthogonality, IFFT/FFT modulation, and Cyclic Prefix mitigation of multipath delay spread.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Multipath Delay Spread and Frequency-Selective Fading:) Tj
T*
(   - In wireless environments, transmitted RF waves reflect from buildings, terrain, and vehicles,) Tj
T*
(   arriving at the receiver across multiple paths with differing propagation delays. The maximum) Tj
T*
(   delay difference is the Delay Spread \(tau_d\).) Tj
T*
(   - In high-speed single-carrier systems, symbol duration Ts is smaller than delay spread \(Ts <) Tj
T*
(   tau_d\), causing overlapping multipath echoes to severely corrupt subsequent symbols) Tj
T*
(   \(Inter-Symbol Interference - ISI\), requiring complex channel equalizers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. OFDM Principles and Subcarrier Orthogonality:) Tj
T*
(   - Parallelization: OFDM divides a wideband high-speed data stream into N parallel low-rate) Tj
T*
(   narrowband subchannels. The symbol duration on each subcarrier expands by N times \(T_sub = N *) Tj
T*
(   Ts >> tau_d\), converting a challenging frequency-selective fading channel into N simple,) Tj
T*
(   flat-fading narrowband subchannels.) Tj
T*
(   - Mathematical Orthogonality Condition: Subcarriers are spaced at minimum frequency intervals) Tj
T*
(   Delta f = 1 / T_sym. The cross-correlation between two distinct subcarriers p and q over symbol) Tj
T*
(   duration T_sym is zero:) Tj
T*
(   \(1 / T_sym\) * integral_{0}^{T_sym} exp\( j * 2 * pi * p * Delta f * t \) * exp\( -j * 2 * pi * q *) Tj
T*
(   Delta f * t \) dt = delta_{p,q}.) Tj
T*
(   - This allows subcarrier frequency spectra to overlap densely without creating Inter-Carrier) Tj
T*
(   Interference \(ICI\), maximizing spectral efficiency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. IFFT/FFT Implementation and Cyclic Prefix \(CP\):) Tj
T*
(   - Digital Generation: The N complex constellation symbols \(QAM\) are mapped directly onto) Tj
T*
(   subcarriers via an Inverse Fast Fourier Transform \(IFFT\) at the transmitter, while an FFT at) Tj
T*
(   the receiver demultiplexes subcarriers simultaneously.) Tj
T*
(   - Cyclic Prefix \(CP\): A copy of the last portion of the OFDM symbol is prepended to the) Tj
T*
(   beginning of the symbol. As long as CP duration T_cp exceeds the channel multipath delay spread) Tj
T*
(   tau_d, multipath echoes from preceding symbols fall harmlessly within the guard interval.) Tj
T*
(   Furthermore, the CP transforms linear channel convolution into circular convolution, allowing) Tj
T*
(   simple single-tap frequency-domain equalization at the receiver.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
