(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the operational mechanisms, performance trade-offs, and typical use cases of serial peripheral interfaces in embedded microcontroller systems: UART, SPI, I2C, and CAN-FD.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Universal Asynchronous Receiver-Transmitter \(UART\):) Tj
T*
(   - Architecture: Asynchronous point-to-point full-duplex communication using two dedicated data) Tj
T*
(   lines: TX \(Transmit\) and RX \(Receive\). No shared clock line is transmitted.) Tj
T*
(   - Synchronization: Both sender and receiver must be pre-configured to identical baud rates) Tj
T*
(   \(e.g., 115200 bps\). Each byte is framed by a Start Bit \(logic low transition triggering) Tj
T*
(   internal clock counter\), 7-8 data bits, optional Parity bit, and 1-2 Stop Bits.) Tj
T*
