(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the principles of Analog-to-Digital Conversion \(ADC\), deriving equations for quantization step size, dynamic range, Signal-to-Quantization-Noise Ratio \(SQNR\), and comparing SAR vs Flash vs Delta-Sigma architectures.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Quantization Theory and Mathematical Derivations:) Tj
T*
(   - An N-bit ADC divides a full-scale continuous analog voltage range V_fs into 2^N discrete) Tj
T*
(   digital codes. The quantization step size \(resolution of 1 LSB\) is:) Tj
T*
(   Delta = V_fs / \(2^N\).) Tj
T*
(   - Quantization Error: The difference between analog input voltage and discretized digital level) Tj
T*
(   is bounded by -Delta/2 <= e_q <= +Delta/2. Assuming uniform distribution over this interval,) Tj
T*
(   error variance \(noise power\) is:) Tj
T*
(   sigma_q^2 = \(1 / Delta\) * integral_{-Delta/2}^{+Delta/2} e^2 de = Delta^2 / 12.) Tj
T*
(   - Derivation of Ideal SQNR: For a full-scale sinusoidal input v\(t\) = \(V_fs / 2\) * sin\(omega *) Tj
T*
(   t\), signal power is P_sig = \(V_fs / 2\)^2 / 2 = V_fs^2 / 8. Expressing V_fs = Delta * 2^N, P_sig) Tj
T*
(   = \(Delta^2 * 2^{2N}\) / 8.) Tj
T*
(   SQNR = P_sig / sigma_q^2 = [ \(Delta^2 * 2^{2N}\) / 8 ] / [ Delta^2 / 12 ] = 1.5 * 2^{2N}.) Tj
T*
(   In decibels: SQNR_dB = 10 * log10\(1.5 * 2^{2N}\) = 10 * log10\(1.5\) + 20 * N * log10\(2\) = 1.76 +) Tj
T*
(   6.02 * N dB.) Tj
T*
(   - Rule of Thumb: Each additional bit of ADC resolution improves signal dynamic range by) Tj
T*
(   approximately 6 dB.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Comparative Architectural Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Flash ADC: Uses 2^N - 1 analog comparators in parallel with a resistor divider ladder.) Tj
T*
(   Evaluates entire conversion in a single clock cycle. Extremely fast \(>several GSa/s\), but) Tj
T*
(   exponential hardware scaling \(10-bit Flash needs 1023 comparators\) consumes immense power and) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
