(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the physical principles of RF Microwave S-parameters \(Scattering Parameters\), explaining S11, S21, S12, S22, their measurement using Vector Network Analyzers \(VNA\), and RF stability circles.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Motivation for Scattering Parameters \(S-Parameters\):) Tj
T*
(   - At low frequencies, two-port networks are characterized using impedance \(Z\), admittance \(Y\),) Tj
T*
(   or hybrid \(H\) parameters based on open-circuit and short-circuit terminal voltage/current) Tj
T*
(   measurements.) Tj
T*
(   - At RF and microwave frequencies, creating perfect open or short circuits is virtually) Tj
T*
(   impossible due to parasitic stray capacitance and lead inductance. Furthermore, short circuits) Tj
T*
(   can induce destructive self-oscillation in active RF transistors. S-parameters characterize) Tj
T*
(   networks using traveling incident \(a\) and reflected/transmitted \(b\) power waves terminated in) Tj
T*
(   matched 50-Ohm loads.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Two-Port S-Parameter Mathematical Definitions:) Tj
T*
(   - The linear two-port relationship: b1 = S11 * a1 + S12 * a2; b2 = S21 * a1 + S22 * a2.) Tj
T*
(   - S11 \(Input Reflection Coefficient\): Ratio of reflected power wave at port 1 to incident wave) Tj
T*
(   at port 1, with port 2 terminated in 50 Ohms: S11 = b1 / a1 | a2=0. Relates directly to Input) Tj
T*
(   Return Loss \(RL = -20 * log10|S11|\) and VSWR.) Tj
T*
(   - S21 \(Forward Transmission Gain\): Ratio of transmitted wave at port 2 to incident wave at port) Tj
T*
(   1: S21 = b2 / a1 | a2=0. Represents power gain or insertion loss.) Tj
T*
(   - S12 \(Reverse Isolation\): Ratio of feedback wave emerging at port 1 due to incident excitation) Tj
T*
(   at port 2: S12 = b1 / a2 | a1=0.) Tj
T*
(   - S22 \(Output Reflection Coefficient\): S22 = b2 / a2 | a1=0. Dictates output impedance match to) Tj
T*
(   antenna or load.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Measurement and RF Circuit Stability:) Tj
T*
(   - Vector Network Analyzer \(VNA\): Employs a synthesized RF sweeper, directional couplers to) Tj
T*
(   separate forward/reverse traveling waves, and coherent down-conversion receivers.) Tj
T*
(   Pre-calibrated using Short-Open-Load-Thru \(SOLT\) standards to mathematically de-embed fixture) Tj
T*
(   parasitics.) Tj
T*
(   - Rollett's Stability Criterion: An RF amplifier is unconditionally stable \(will not oscillate) Tj
T*
(   for any passive load/source impedance\) if Rollett's factor K > 1 and auxiliary factor |Delta| <) Tj
T*
(   1, where K = \( 1 - |S11|^2 - |S22|^2 + |Delta|^2 \) / \( 2 * |S12 * S21| \), and Delta = S11 * S22) Tj
T*
(   - S12 * S21.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
